{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>You shall utterly destroy all the places.</b> The verse speaks of implements that were used in idolatrous worship, for the places themselves cannot be destroyed. Moreover, land is not subject to prohibition, as is explained further on." "<b>Et their gods upon the mountains.</b> Our rabbis interpreted: and not the mountains — their gods." "<b>Et their gods.</b> Defective in vav, and it is linked back to the preceding. And if you ask: their gods upon the mountains where the nations served their gods there."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:30.168615387Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}